title: Azure Firewall: IP Configuration
agents: azure
catalog: cloud/azure
license: GPLv2
distribution: kuhn-ruess
description:
 This check monitors an IP configuration (data plane or management) of an
 Azure Firewall. It shows the provisioning state, the private IP, the public
 IP address and the name of the public IP resource. {Succeeded} is {OK},
 {Failed} and {Canceled} are {CRIT}, every other state is {WARN}.

 The private IP, the public IP address and the public IP resource are stored
 when the service is discovered. If one of them changes, the service is
 {CRIT} until the service is discovered again, which accepts the new
 addresses. The state can be changed with the rule "Azure Extra: Firewall IP
 configuration". Services discovered with an older version of the plugin have
 no stored addresses and need one rediscovery to enable the change detection.

item:
 The firewall name and the IP configuration name, joined by "_".

discovery:
 One service is created for each IP configuration of a firewall.
